/*
 * GameplayHud — layout only. The wrist menu: four panel-open buttons in a single column on a panel
 * strapped to the support forearm. Colours, spacing steps and type sizes resolve from Tokens/Base.
 *
 * THIS FILE'S NAME IS LOAD-BEARING. The bootstrapper resolves a screen's own sheet by DOCUMENT
 * NAME, and the per-screen sheet is optional by design — so a document whose sheet is missing
 * renders unstyled and reports itself healthy. The health readout's rules used to live here after
 * its markup had already moved to GameplayStats.uxml, which meant the health bar had no height and
 * no fill colour and nothing reported it. They now live in GameplayStats.uss next to the document
 * that owns them, and ScreenStyleSheetReachabilityEditModeTests fails if they drift apart again.
 *
 * ── One column, not a 2x2 grid ──────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * A grid was the first attempt and does not fit. At 240 px the panel's content box is 192 px
 * (.hs-screen takes 24 px of padding a side); two buttons per row with 5 px margins leaves 86 px
 * each, and .hs-button's own 22 px of horizontal padding leaves 42 px of text at a 28 px font.
 * "Inventory" needs roughly 130 px, so every label would have wrapped or clipped.
 *
 * One column at 300 px wide gives 242 px per button and 198 px of text — clear of the longest
 * label ("Shared crate", ~165 px) — and 350 px tall holds four 64 px controls plus margins.
 */

.gh-actions {
    flex-direction: column;
    flex-grow: 1;
    justify-content: center;
}

/* Full width of the content box; 5 px top and bottom puts 10 mm between adjacent targets, inside
   the FPV report's 8-12 mm minimum for adjacent hit targets. Live validation flagged the old row
   as possibly violating this between "Crafting" and "Shared crate", so it is explicit here rather
   than incidental. */
.gh-action {
    margin-left: 5px;
    margin-right: 5px;
    margin-top: 5px;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
}

/* Collapsed unless the player turns their wrist toward their face.
 *
 * Applied to the ACTIONS container, never to bv-screen-root: UiToolkitScreenController.SetVisible
 * writes an inline style.display onto the root, and a UI Toolkit inline style outranks every USS
 * rule, so a display rule there would be silently discarded and the menu would ride the player's
 * wrist permanently open. The root's paint is suppressed separately with hs-screen--unpainted so
 * no empty plate is left strapped to the forearm. */
.gh-actions--collapsed {
    display: none;
}
